 /* Second members of V+V compounds (Smeets 2007 \u00a729.1, pp. 316-317). These are
    verb roots, not slot fillers. Smeets notes that the position they occupy is the
    same position taken by the slot 32 suffixes -nie- prps and -k\u00fcnu- pfps, so they
    compete positionally with slot 32 without belonging to it.
    "min" is the minimum number of characters that must precede the form, to stop
    short forms firing inside a root (e.g. uam- inside duam-). */
 {f:"ntuku",gloss:"put/insert",min:2,note:"aspectual second member; -ntuku- after a vowel, -tuku- otherwise (\u00a729.1). Sp. loan example: gana-ntuku- 'to continue to earn'"},
 {f:"tuku", gloss:"put/insert",min:2,note:"aspectual second member (\u00a729.1); cf. kim-tuku- 'to have come to know bit by bit'"},
 {f:"k\u00fcnu", gloss:"let be",    min:2,note:"compounding verb root k\u00fcnu- 'to let be'; cf. grammaticalized -k\u00fcnu- pfps at slot 32 (\u00a729.1)"},
 {f:"kon",  gloss:"enter/begin",min:3,note:"aspectual second member (\u00a729.1): a\u00f1i-kon-k\u00fcle- 'to be scorching', wiri-kon-k\u00fcle- 'to be writing', kim-kon- 'to find out'. Often followed by -(k\u00fc)le- st28. Also purely lexical: \u00fctr\u00fcf-kon- 'to fall in'"},
 {f:"p\u00fcra", gloss:"go up",     min:3,note:"aspectual second member (\u00a729.1): kim-p\u00fcra-me- 'to realize'. A linking \u00f1 may be inserted after a vowel-final first member (\u00a78.1.8)"},
 {f:"naq",  gloss:"go down",   min:3,note:"productive aspectual (\u00a729.1) marking a process reaching completion: ng\u00fck\u00fcf-naq- 'to die down', t\u00fcng-naq- 'to quiet down'"},
 {f:"uam",  gloss:"need/want", min:3,note:"productive aspectual (\u00a729.1): half-completed process with intransitives (angi-uam- 'to become dry'), half-finished situation with transitives (ap-\u00fcm-uam- 'to have half finished'). Beware the root duam-"}
